# SRG-APP-000120-WSR-000070  -  CAT II
# The log information from the web server must be protected from
# unauthorized deletion.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000120-WSR-000070
group:           V-206370
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000164
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    The application withholds the in-product delete path from the
                 general-purpose roles and keeps the internal indexes that hold Splunk
                 Web's records out of every role's delete scope.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [role_user] delete_by_keyword absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] delete_by_keyword absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_can_delete] deleteIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|;)[[:space:]]*_
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] deleteIndexesAllowed matches tls1\.2 -> authorize.conf [role_can_delete] deleteIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|;)[[:space:]]*_
vendor:          authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] deleteIndexesAllowed https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/authorize.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Delete permissions on the Splunk log directory - SPLK-CL-000190 implements
                 this at the operating system layer
external:        Which roles the organization authorizes to run the delete command

citation:        The deleteIndexesAllowed condition carries the wildcard inversion
                 corrected on SRG-APP-000119-AU-000110. log.access_maxfiles min 1 and
                 log.error_maxfiles min 1 are removed: the rotated-backup count appears in
                 neither the check text nor the product STIG fix text, and what it governs
                 - how many generations rotation keeps before discarding the oldest - is
                 authorized retention behavior rather than protection from unauthorized
                 deletion, which SPLK-CL-000190 assigns to file permissions.
finding:         A general-purpose role holds delete_by_keyword, or a role's
                 deleteIndexesAllowed list reaches the internal indexes, so the indexed
                 Splunk Web records can be deleted from search results by an unprivileged
                 account.
